contentText:
Luis Maldonado remembers being about 5 years old when he listened for the first time to a Foreigner song. It was the late &#8217;70s in Mexico, in the border city of Nogales, Sonora, where he could dial the family&#8217;s radio into the rock stations in Arizona.

&#8220;It was &#8216;Feels Like the First Time,&#8217; and I just remember hearing all those sounds, you know, the keyboards, the big guitars &#8212; I&#8217;m like, &#8216;Wow, listen to that sound!&#8217; That&#8217;s kind of what made me obsessed with music,&#8221; he tells Billboard Español . Little did he know that, decades later, he would end up fronting the Rock and Roll Hall of Famer band.

